=== UART drain-stop flag: ThreadSanitizer reproduction (2026-10-21) ===
finding: the drain thread's stop flag is a field of a main-thread stack object
         (FF_UartDrain_t drain) whose address is passed to pthread_create; the main
         thread writes it (tests/unit/test_link_uart.c:304) and the drain thread reads
         it (tests/unit/test_link_uart.c:97). No mutex, C11 atomic or condition variable
         is used between them, so 'volatile' does NOT provide inter-thread
         synchronization: this is a C11 data race (undefined behaviour).
tooling: gcc -fsanitize=thread (already present; no install)
method: out-of-tree copy of the tree; the scratch copy forces the send-failure path
        (1 ms deadline instead of 1 s) so the main thread actually writes the flag.
        The repository was NOT modified; the scratch copy was removed afterwards.
result: TSan data race, read at test_link_uart.c:97 by the drain thread vs previous write at
        test_link_uart.c:304 by the main thread, on the main thread's stack:
WARNING: ThreadSanitizer: data race (pid=3008669)
  Read of size 1 at 0x7ffffffedf00 by thread T2:
    #0 uart_delayed_drain tests/unit/test_link_uart.c:97 (test_link_uart+0x296a) (BuildId: 83101ae05b419bac2f74d361ff276a63553f463e)

  Previous write of size 1 at 0x7ffffffedf00 by main thread:
    #0 test_uart_framing_split_coalesced_timeout_and_bounds tests/unit/test_link_uart.c:304 (test_link_uart+0x3e8c) (BuildId: 83101ae05b419bac2f74d361ff276a63553f463e)
    #1 main tests/unit/test_link_uart.c:373 (test_link_uart+0x5f72) (BuildId: 83101ae05b419bac2f74d361ff276a63553f463e)

  As if synchronized via sleep:
    #0 nanosleep ../../../../src/libsanitizer/tsan/tsan_interceptors_posix.cpp:396 (libtsan.so.2+0x59dcf) (BuildId: 66d37dc704b813df6c813b77217284deb43a0042)
    #1 uart_delayed_drain tests/unit/test_link_uart.c:96 (test_link_uart+0x28d3) (BuildId: 83101ae05b419bac2f74d361ff276a63553f463e)

  Location is stack of main thread.

  Thread T2 (tid=3008673, running) created by main thread at:
    #0 pthread_create ../../../../src/libsanitizer/tsan/tsan_interceptors_posix.cpp:1078 (libtsan.so.2+0x5cb02) (BuildId: 66d37dc704b813df6c813b77217284deb43a0042)
    #1 test_uart_framing_split_coalesced_timeout_and_bounds tests/unit/test_link_uart.c:293 (test_link_uart+0x3dfc) (BuildId: 83101ae05b419bac2f74d361ff276a63553f463e)
    #2 main tests/unit/test_link_uart.c:373 (test_link_uart+0x5f72) (BuildId: 83101ae05b419bac2f74d361ff276a63553f463e)

SUMMARY: ThreadSanitizer: data race tests/unit/test_link_uart.c:97 in uart_delayed_drain
note:  the race is on the failure path only (the main thread writes the flag only when
        the send fails), so the nominal suite run does not exercise it.
disposition: registered OPEN/deferred for owner triage; the earlier 'the drain thread
        cannot hang' wording in the handover and in FRICK-REVIEW-0421 is superseded
        by this finding.

