=== UART drain-stop race: BEFORE/AFTER ThreadSanitizer pair (2026-10-21, correction round) ===
correction: tests/unit/test_link_uart.c — the drain thread's stop flag is now protected by a
             pthread mutex (the project builds as C99, CMakeLists.txt:30-32, where <stdatomic.h>
             is not part of the language, so pthread synchronization is used instead of
             'volatile'). The flag stays in the same stack object, the mutex is initialized
             before pthread_create and destroyed after the join, and the stop request is still
             made only when the send fails. No production code, watchdog policy, refresh
             timing, coverage or expected result was changed.

harness (identical for both runs, out-of-tree copy; the repository was NOT modified):
  gcc -fsanitize=thread -g -O1, TSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=0
  scratch-only modification: the big transfer deadline is 1 ms instead of 1 s, so the
  send fails and the main thread requests the drain stop (the reproducer).

